@@ -8840,3 +8840,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - **Adversarial round (`results/arc3_gap4_arc2_adversarial_verify.json`): 5/5 CONFIRMED, worst severity minor.** All numbers bit-exact; all 56 transcripts leak-clean (first round where the no-oracle invariant is AUDITED, not asserted). Load-bearing finding: **the decay is honest induction strain, not collapse-to-recall** — demo-overfit rises 10.3% → 50% (memorization predicts the opposite signature) and the maximally-exposed task (16b78196, content-identical 5-years-public ARC-1-eval reuse) fails completely at demo_fit 0.0. Corollary stamped into the record: ARC-1's 0.897 precision is an UPPER BOUND on genuine induction; the probe is "reduced-exposure, increased-difficulty", never "held-out" (evaluation2 is public-era; 2/23 tasks are verbatim ARC-1-eval reuses). The one live rerank signal: a prediction 1/493 cells from gold that GRADED min-hamming promoted to rank 1 where the exact-match gate missed — exact-match gating is too brittle on hard tasks.
 - **Ledger (`ops/verifier_gaps.md` GAP-4): calibrated two-point claim + panel-ranked next moves** — (1) k=2–3 independent-induction agreement gate (micro-evidence: agreed pairs gold 3/3 vs 0.50 unconditional); (2) graded execution-energy gate (min-hamming ≤ 0.005), validated on ARC-1 first; (3) adaptive iteration caps + ≥600s timeouts (67% of codex-seconds burned on never-perfect tasks); (4) local open-weight generator arm; (5) the 400-task run deferred until (1)/(2) land — the gate is structurally inert where the base generator is weak, so scale cannot help the rerank framing.
 - 2026-06-10: FOURTH ARC-AGI-3 game first-solve: solve level-1 of the next-easiest NON-SPATIAL game (tn36-ef4dde99 / su15-1944f8ab / dc22 are candidates) via the perception -> induced-model -> goal-predicate -> exploit loop that produced the r11l (exp3946), lp85 (exp3954), and sc25 (exp3966) solves. A FOURTH distinct solved game raises generalization 3->4 (robustness of the method). Real-env-confirmed; pick the game empirically by L0 action budget + inducibility, do NOT hardcode the win from source. AVOID vc33's PSPACE spatial trap (see prior_failures). Where a delta is ambiguous, the SOTA local GGUF may propose object semantics; perception is PRIMARILY deterministic numpy. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: fourth_game_no_solve_budget_exceeded; results/experiment_3981_fourth_game_first_solve.json
+- 2026-06-10: ArcMemo SOLVE-transfer (self-learning MANDATE; extends exp3970's induction-cost transfer win to the SOLVE loop): exp3970 showed NL concept-memory reuse cuts INDUCTION cost across games. This tests whether the SAME concept memory makes a NEW game's SOLVE cheaper — does retrieving the banked solved-game concepts ('select-then-place' r11l, 'permute-set' lp85, 'pattern-match-then-navigate' sc25, + the 4th game from exp3981) reduce the ACTIONS/ATTEMPTS to solve the 4th game vs a cold-start solver with no memory? Two arms at equal perception: (A) cold-start, (B) concept-memory-seeded. This is Tier-2 constraint memory (research-program.md) in the SOLVE loop, the self-learning datum that compounds across games. POSITIVE CONTROL: the sequence must share structure (>=2 select/place-family games) or transfer is impossible by construction (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK). (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: arcmemo_solve_transfer_2668to17_actions; results/experiment_3982_arcmemo_solve_transfer.json
